# Form Requirements

This file describes who you are and what forms you fill, so the
automation can decide if a form qualifies and what values to use.

Edit this file with your own information before running the script.

## Who I Am (Test Persona)

The values below are used when a form asks about you.

- **Name:** Your Name
- **Email:** your@email.com
- **Phone:** +15551234567
- **Organization:** Your Organization

If a question doesn't match any of the above, the automation will
generate a plausible fake value appropriate for the form type.

## What Kinds of Forms I Fill

Describe the types of forms you typically fill out (e.g. event
registrations, surveys, sign-up forms). The automation uses this to
decide if a form qualifies.

## Rules

- Only fill forms you would realistically sign up for.
- Answer required questions first.
- Never write placeholder text into required fields.
- For multiple-choice fields, always pick a real option.
- For checkboxes, pick 1–3 real options.

## What NOT to Fill

Skip the entire form if any question asks for:
- Passwords or credentials
- Social security numbers or national IDs
- Credit card or bank details

## How to Use

1. Copy this file to `requirements.md` (or edit it in place)
2. Fill in your identity and rules
3. Run `wa check-requirements <form-url>` to test
4. Run `wa run --loop` to monitor and auto-fill qualifying forms